From: sadatdaniel <sadatdaniel@yahoo.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: samsung: abox: initialize frequency before logging

abox_change_cpu_gear logs freq even when the selected gear is unchanged.
On that path freq has never been assigned. The aa6 suspend trace therefore
prints req=1636958208kHz although no such QoS update occurred.

Compute the selected frequency before the conditional update so unchanged
requests are logged correctly. Keep the actual QoS update conditional.
This is a diagnostic fix, not a demonstrated fix for the delayed freeze.

--- a/sound/soc/samsung/abox/abox.c
+++ b/sound/soc/samsung/abox/abox.c
@@ -3630,9 +3630,9 @@ static void abox_change_cpu_gear(struct device *dev, struct abox_data *data)
 		pm_runtime_get(dev);
 	}
 
+	freq = (gear <= ARRAY_SIZE(data->pm_qos_aud)) ?
+			data->pm_qos_aud[gear - 1] : 0;
 	if (data->cpu_gear != gear) {
-		freq = (gear <= ARRAY_SIZE(data->pm_qos_aud)) ?
-				data->pm_qos_aud[gear - 1] : 0;
 		pm_qos_update_request(&abox_pm_qos_aud, freq);
 	}
 
